# Shaping cases on the committed Inter metrics subset (tests/fonts/), in
# HarfBuzz's .tests format: font;options;code points;expected. Expectations
# are HarfBuzz's output with glyph ids; `?` asks record_oracle.py
# --fill-expected to write it. A `# id: <name>` comment names the next case.
# Inter's metrics subset keeps hmtx, cmap, GSUB, GPOS and glyph bounding
# boxes, but no outlines, `name` or `post` (see tools/font_subset.mjs).

